# CLAUDE.md — <brain>

Personal knowledge-base brain repo. Mixed-authorship: owner writes high-signal content, agents append captures from external sources, an external library holds collected sources, and regenerable derivations live alongside.

## Realms — read carefully before writing

| Realm        | Path              | Who writes           | Rule                                                           |
| ------------ | ----------------- | -------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **owner**    | <owner-realm>/    | owner only           | Agents may **read**, must not write.                           |
| **captured** | <captured-realm>/ | agents (append-only) | Files are **immutable** after first commit.                    |
| **external** | <external-realm>/ | owner + agents       | Prefer extracted markdown + SOURCES.md pointers over binaries. |
| **derived**  | <derived-realm>/  | agents               | Regenerable. Safe to delete and rebuild.                       |

## Non-Negotiable Rules

- Realm boundaries are enforced by `task verify`; do not bypass.
- Captured realm is append-only; never edit existing files there.
- Privacy posture: secret scan + banned-string scan run pre-commit.
- This document is intentionally mirrored in `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md`.

## Verification Gate

```bash
task verify
```

Pre-commit hook runs the cheap subset (secrets, mirror, immutability, source-READMEs).

## Pointers

- `docs/` — convention docs (requests/planning/plans/implementation).
- `<owner-realm>/` — your authored content. Agents do not write here without explicit ask.
- `<captured-realm>/` — raw exports. Each source has a README declaring producer/cadence/schema.
- `<derived-realm>/` — agent-generated. Safe to delete and regenerate.
- `<external-realm>/` — collected external content. Use `SOURCES.md` pointers for large binaries.
